      "template": "TITLE",
      "narration": "JavaScript runs one task at a time. The event loop coordinates when waiting callbacks can run.",
      "estimatedDurationSec": 7,
      "visualProps": {
        "title": "The JavaScript event loop",
        "subtitle": "One call stack, tasks and microtasks"
      }
    },
    {
      "sceneId": "stack_30",
      "template": "STACK_QUEUE",
      "narration": "Function calls enter the stack, and the newest finishes first. Long tasks keep other callbacks waiting.",
      "estimatedDurationSec": 8,
      "visualProps": {
        "title": "One call stack",
        "items": [
          "main()",
          "calculate()",
          "format()"
        ],
        "layout": "STACK"
      }
    },
    {
      "sceneId": "flow_30",
      "template": "FLOWCHART",
      "narration": "After the current task, the browser drains microtasks before running a later task, such as a timer.",
      "estimatedDurationSec": 8,
      "visualProps": {
